# Caddy config for the minimal single-VM deployment (docs/minimal-deployment.md).
# Domains come from deploy/.env via the compose service's environment.
#
# The VM serves the API only. The SPA, on the apex and every tenant subdomain,
# is S3 + CloudFront (infra/frontend.tf, docs/decisions.md §278), and since
# §364 nothing on this VM builds or serves it. So this file names no platform
# host but api.<domain>: those names resolve to CloudFront, and a site block
# for one would only have Caddy failing HTTP-01 for a certificate it can never
# get.
#
# TLS is automatic per-host HTTP-01: every hostname here and in tenants.caddy
# gets its own Let's Encrypt certificate, so each must resolve to this VM.

{
	email {$ACME_EMAIL}
}

# Backend API. The SPA is built with PUBLIC_API_URL=https://{$API_DOMAIN};
# CORS for the tenant subdomains is the backend's job (FEOH_CORS_PRODUCTION_DOMAIN).
{$API_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy api:8000
}

# A customer's vanity host (docs/founder-runbooks/custom-domain-provisioning.md
# § 3a). Its certificate is issued here, because CloudFront would need one per
# customer; the page itself comes from CloudFront.
#
#   - /api keeps the vanity Host: that is how the backend resolves a
#     registered custom domain to its tenant.
#   - Everything else is the SPA, fetched from the platform domain. CloudFront
#     refuses a Host that is not one of its alternate names, so Host and SNI
#     are rewritten to {$APP_DOMAIN}; the page is the same build every host
#     serves, and the SPA reads its tenant from the browser's own location.
#     CloudFront's response-headers policy sets HSTS and the other security
#     headers, and they pass through unchanged.
(vanity) {
	@api path /api /api/*
	handle @api {
		reverse_proxy api:8000
	}
	handle {
		reverse_proxy https://{$APP_DOMAIN} {
			header_up Host {$APP_DOMAIN}
			transport http {
				tls_server_name {$APP_DOMAIN}
			}
		}
	}
}

# One block per vanity host, `<host> { import vanity }`, in the per-VM
# tenants.caddy (gitignored; deploy.sh seeds it from tenants.caddy.example).
import tenants.caddy
